From 410403d6aaa6c39494d48dd3d003af9aebb12b4f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 10:58:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] i18n: translate the firmware, Data Export and USB/storage
 strings into all 24 languages

Backlog [P3] was the firmware page (RFWU_1-31, English-seeded since v2.3.1). An
audit of all 25 packs found the same gap on two more Reaper pages, so this does
the lot: 98 keys x 24 languages = 2352 strings.

  RFWU_1-31   Reaper_Firmware.asp   the backlog item
  RANL_*      Reaper_Analytics.asp  Data Export, 46 keys, never translated
  RDST_43-63  Reaper_USB.asp + Reaper_Storage.asp, 19 keys
  RQOS_123    Reaper_QoS.asp        added earlier today
  RWFP_14     Reaper_WiFiPro.asp

DELIBERATELY LEFT ENGLISH (15 keys), so a later pass does not "fix" them:
product and feature names (Warden, Gatekeeper), feed names (FireHOL Level 1,
Spamhaus DROP), acronyms (AQM, WISP, Wi-Fi, HTTP + HTTPS), literal IP examples,
the Splunk field names Index/Sourcetype, URL, and "HW Classful" - an engine
display name that standing rule 19 pins to English everywhere user-facing.

FOUND, NOT FIXED: NetworkTools_PktCap{,_desc,_iface,_dur,_snap,_filter,_btn} are
in all 25 dicts but NO page references them - a packet-capture UI that was never
wired up. Left alone and reported rather than translated.

RULE-29 HARDENING in the same pass. A dict token inside a '...' JS string is a
mine: the day that translation gains an apostrophe the page is a syntax error in
that language only (the v1.8.6a EU field breakage). The 2026-07-28 sweep
converted the pages that existed then; a source scan found 14 sites since added
or missed - 8 in menuTrees/menuTree.js (menu-name comparisons) and 2 lines in
Reaper_Conn.asp - now backticks. None of those translations carries an
apostrophe today, so this is prevention, not a repair.

VERIFIED, no build required:
- 475 page/language combinations (19 pages x 25 packs) COMPILE: every <#token#>
  substituted with that language's real value and the inline JS parsed. This is
  the source-level twin of the reaper_langcheck.py build gate, which can only
  run post-build because it matches numeric tokens.
- Lockstep intact: all 25 dicts 6295 lines, identical key ORDER (the build
  line-indexes tokens, so a shifted line silently remaps every string after it).
- UTF-8, no BOM, no CRLF - and the apply step refuses any value carrying a
  backtick, ${, newline, or a quote that would close its own string context.
- Seven values are byte-identical to English on purpose (Status, Destination,
  Endpoint, Mode, Updates, Variant, Model in the languages that spell them the
  same); each is allowlisted so the gate stays meaningful.

Untranslated Reaper strings remaining: none.

NOT BUILT. Owes an on-device look at the long strings in the tightest chrome -
the German and Finnish firmware-page descriptions are the widest.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
